{
  "abstract": "We assess whether the weak mixing angle provides a redundant test of the selected MTT gauge profile. At the same scale and in the same scheme, the weak angle is an exact rational function of the GUT-normalized weak-to-hypercharge overlap ratio. For the selected SMDR profile at the top-mass matching scale, this gives 0.2346644 with propagated uncertainty 0.0000433. Because the overlap ratio was itself obtained from the measured hypercharge and weak couplings, this equality is an algebraic round trip rather than a held-out prediction. Supplying an absolute weak coupling from the Fermi constant and W-boson mass does not remove that circularity. A genuine redundancy test requires an MTT source theorem selecting the ratio without electroweak gauge data, followed by independent common-scheme transport.",
